      "updated": 1790352636034,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Enabling technology\" - why can we write code like the string calculator taught us?\n    - small incremental steps, getting feedback, etc.\n\n\n1. You ship the environment with the app.\n    - \"Container\" as in \"put everything you need in this box and give it to the environment\"\n    - the environment that is going to run your container needs a \"Container Runtime\"\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Enabling technology\" - why can we write code like the string calculator taught us?\n    - small incremental steps, getting feedback, etc.\n\n\n1. You ship the environment with the app.\n    - \"Container\" as in \"put everything you need in this box and give it to the environment\"\n    - the environment that is going to run your container needs a \"Container Runtime\"\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
